              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260807172421.3875982-1-usama.arif@linux.dev/",
              "subject": "[PATCH v2] squashfs: avoid thundering-herd cache wakeups",
              "date": "2026-08-07T17:24:56Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch modifies the squashfs cache handling to avoid 'thundering herd' wakeups, which occur when multiple tasks are woken up simultaneously due to a single event. The patch makes waits exclusive and enqueues them while holding the cache lock, ensuring that a concurrent lookup either sees the waiter queued or the waiter sees the block published. This change reduces CPU usage spikes caused by frequent wakeups and improves system performance.",
